            9. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming strawberry means real fruit</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Many strawberry powders contain no strawberry at all. Gold Standard Delicious Strawberry uses flavoring, citric acid and Red 40 lake. If real fruit matters to you, look for dried or freeze-dried strawberry or strawberry powder in the ingredient list itself.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Missing the dye on the label</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Red 40 appears in some popular strawberry tubs, including Gold Standard and Isopure. It is FDA-approved and used in tiny amounts, but if you or your children avoid synthetic dyes, read the full ingredient list instead of relying on the front of the tub.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating a meal shake as a protein powder</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Ka'Chava Strawberry has about 240 calories per serving because it is built to replace a meal. Drinking it alongside meals as a protein top-up adds calories quickly. For post-workout protein, a strawberry whey isolate gives similar protein for less than half the calories.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing two-scoop and one-scoop servings directly</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Naked, Orgain and Ka'Chava use two-scoop servings while the isolates use one. Compare protein per serving and calories per serving, not scoops, or a two-scoop tub will look either better or worse than it really is.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the biggest tub of the most divisive flavor</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Strawberry splits buyers more than any other mainstream flavor. Start with the smallest tub or a sample before buying 5 lb, especially for flavoring-based powders that some people describe as candy-like.
              </p>
            </div>
